The exporter keeps the source's 30 binary statements, copies their participant
votes exactly, and replaces participant identifiers with positional
pseudonyms. It recomputes per-statement vote counts from those votes. Its own
seeded PCA and k-means clustering derive the two participant clusters, their
centers, and comment extremity; divisiveness repeats extremity. None of these
derived values come from the source's group assignments or summary
statistics. The exporter also adds empty evaluation-mask fields and
provenance metadata.

